-- ############################ READ THIS ############################
-- Mechanically converted, not hand-verified. Quest IDs and coordinates
-- came from a text-processing pass over a real, currently-maintained
-- guide (see Credits & License at the bottom of this file), not from
-- someone playing this route and confirming each step in-game.
--
-- Before trusting any of it, run:  /tuff verify
-- That checks every ID in this file against QuestieDB and reports
-- anything it can't find. Report problems found in-game back into this
-- file the normal way (see CONTRIBUTING.md) rather than discarding it.
-- ###################################################################
--
-- Tauren starting zone (Bloodhoof Village -> Mulgore) through the full
-- Horde 1-60 leveling path, converging with the general Horde path
-- through The Barrens from level ~12 onward. This is a SEPARATE,
-- self-contained route from the existing Orc/Troll ONSLAUGHT-sourced
-- Routes/Horde/Solo/*.lua set - it does not share that system's Leg()
-- plumbing (which is Orc/Troll-specific by design, see Solo/Init.lua's
-- header), so it carries zero risk to that route. Added because there
-- was previously no Tauren-starting route in this addon at all.
--
-- Every step carries the same schema documented in the header of
-- Routes/Horde/Durotar.lua. Steps that only apply to one class or one
-- other Horde race (this shared route also carries some Orc/Troll/
-- Scourge-specific steps inherited from the source guide's shared
-- zones) carry `class`/`races` filters the normal way.
--
-- SCOPE DECISIONS MADE DURING CONVERSION (same methodology as
-- Routes/Alliance/*.lua - see those files for the full rationale)
--
-- The source guide branches at several points; one canonical path was
-- picked per the same rules (avoid a non-default class requirement,
-- first-listed when tied). Season of Discovery content and alternate
-- AoE-grinding leveling methods were skipped entirely as out of scope.
-- A small number of steps carry a note starting with raw source syntax
-- where no plain-language annotation existed to fall back to.
--
-- KNOWN GAP: about 24 steps use a continent-level zone reference
-- ("Kalimdor" / "Eastern Kingdoms") for wide-area transitions (entering
-- an instance portal, crossing a zone boundary) that this addon's zone
-- table doesn't have a uiMapID for - those steps' arrows won't resolve
-- until that's added. Everything else about those steps (quest tracking,
-- text) still works.

